</style></head><body><main class="shell"><header class="top"><div class="brand">I Love My Body<small>NILESH YADAV · PRIVATE PATIENT JOURNEY</small></div><div class="tools"><button class="btn" onclick="window.print()">Print / PDF</button><a class="btn" href="?logout=1">Log out</a></div></header><nav class="nav"><button class="active" data-panel="compare">1. Pharmacy = ILMB</button><button data-panel="path">2. Actual ILMB Path</button><button data-panel="reports">3. Reports</button><button data-panel="numbers">4. Measurements</button><button data-panel="science">5. Background</button></nav><div class="stage">
<section id="compare" class="panel active"><div class="section"><div class="ey">THE CORE RULE</div><h2>Same required body result. Two different routes.</h2><div class="rule">PHARMACY RESULT = ILMB RESULT <small>Equality is claimed only when the same physiological endpoint is measured and matched. Different mechanism is allowed; unproven equality stays marked NOT YET ESTABLISHED.</small></div><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare"><thead><tr><th>Required body result</th><th>Pharmacy route</th><th>Collateral / side-effect path</th><th>ILMB route to the same result</th><th>How we prove equality</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower recurrent ischemic / thrombotic risk</td><td><b>Clopidogrel 75 mg</b><br>P2Y12 inhibition → platelet aggregation ↓<br><br><b>Aspirin 150 mg</b><br>COX-1 inhibition → TXA₂ ↓ → platelet aggregation ↓</td><td class="harm">The same antiplatelet effect reduces normal hemostasis, increasing bleeding/bruising/GI bleeding risk; rare serious adverse effects also exist.</td><td>Keep antiplatelet therapy unchanged while ILMB reduces measurable non-platelet contributors to total vascular risk: BP load, triglyceride-rich particles, atherogenic burden, inactivity, endothelial/metabolic stress, and unresolved perfusion questions.</td><td class="proof">For this endpoint, ILMB equality is <b>NOT YET ESTABLISHED</b>. We can measure risk contributors, but cannot claim the same antiplatelet protection without direct evidence of equivalent recurrence protection.<br><span class="tag">SUPPORTIVE ROUTE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower blood pressure / vascular resistance</td><td><b>Amlodipine 5 mg</b><br>L-type Ca²⁺ blockade → arterial relaxation.<br><br><b>Atenolol 50 mg</b><br>β1 blockade → HR/workload ↓.</td><td class="harm">Edema, dizziness, hypotension; bradycardia, fatigue and suppressed exercise-HR response can occur.</td><td>Measure and modify the actual non-drug determinants in Nilesh: sodium/fluid input, sleep/autonomic state, conditioning, activity and vascular load.</td><td class="proof">Compare 7-day mean SBP/DBP and resting pulse before/after a controlled ILMB intervention. Equality means the same required BP/HR output is reached reproducibly.<br><span class="tag pink">DIRECTLY TESTABLE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower triglyceride-rich particles</td><td><b>Fenofibrate 160 mg</b><br>PPARα activation → TG clearance ↑.</td><td class="harm">Liver-enzyme rise, muscle injury, reversible creatinine rise and gallstones; muscle risk rises with statin combination.</td><td>Quantify Nilesh’s weighed food chemistry + movement/workload → reduce verified hepatic TG substrate and increase measured utilisation → hold intervention constant → repeat fasting TG.</td><td class="proof">Equality means the required fasting TG reduction is achieved and sustained, without unacceptable collateral burden. Calculate Nilesh’s ΔTG / verified Δinput.<br><span class="tag pink">DIRECTLY TESTABLE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Lower atherogenic LDL / apoB burden</td><td><b>Atorvastatin 40 mg</b><br>HMG-CoA reductase inhibition → LDL clearance ↑.</td><td class="harm">Myopathy/muscle injury and liver-enzyme abnormalities can occur; rare rhabdomyolysis is documented.</td><td>Use weighed food chemistry, intestinal/substrate pattern, hepatic substrate supply, body composition and activity to lower the same measured lipid outputs by a different route.</td><td class="proof">Compare LDL-C, non-HDL-C and apoB before/after a controlled ILMB block. Equality is endpoint equality, not HMG-CoA molecular equivalence.<br><span class="tag pink">DIRECTLY TESTABLE</span></td></tr>
<tr><td class="goal">Meet nutrient/cofactor requirement without excess</td><td><b>Cod liver oil / Neurobion</b><br>Provide nutrient/cofactor exposure through fixed formulations.</td><td class="harm">Wrong identity or unnecessary excess can add interaction or toxicity burden; formulation matters.</td><td>Exact label chemistry + diet chemistry + measured deficiency/need → calculate only the required nutrient input from food and/or supplement source.</td><td class="proof">Repeat the relevant biomarker and symptom/function output. No equality claim until exact product chemistry and requirement are known.<br><span class="tag">BLOCKED UNTIL VERIFIED</span></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section id="path" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">ACTUAL ILMB PATH</div><h2>For every pharmacy result, ILMB has to reach the same measurable output.</h2><p class="lead">The patient should not see abstract “targets”. Each route ends with a number that decides whether ILMB matched, failed, or needs modification.</p><div class="paths">
<details class="path" open><summary><b>01</b><strong>BP / vascular resistance</strong><span>Same output as amlodipine/atenolol goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>7 days; morning + evening; seated 5 min; 2 BP readings 1 min apart + pulse.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Weighed sodium/fluid intake, sleep, activity, autonomic symptoms, edema/dizziness.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ILMB intervention</b><p>Change one measured abnormal contributor only; hold other inputs steady.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat the same 7-day BP/pulse protocol.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Equality test</b><p>Same required SBP/DBP/pulse output reached reproducibly with acceptable burden.</p></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>02</b><strong>Triglycerides</strong><span>Same output as fenofibrate goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>Repeat fasting TG/non-HDL/apoB and liver/kidney safety panel.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>3 normal weighed food/drink/supplement days → IFCT/USDA → chemical inputs; movement/workload baseline.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ILMB intervention</b><p>Change one verified substrate/activity input and hold it steady.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat fasting TG with the same pre-test conditions.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Equality test</b><p>Required TG reduction matched; compute Nilesh’s own ΔTG/Δinput.</p></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>03</b><strong>LDL / apoB burden</strong><span>Same output as atorvastatin goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>Verify current LDL method; obtain LDL-C, non-HDL-C and apoB where available.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Use the same weighed food chemistry and activity/body-composition data.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ILMB intervention</b><p>Alter one verified intestinal/substrate/metabolic route.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat the same lipid outputs.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Equality test</b><p>Required lipid endpoint matched; mechanism may differ.</p></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>04</b><strong>Brain perfusion / function</strong><span>Protect the actual tissue outcome</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>Resolve current MCA flow/collaterals/perfusion + bilateral grip, strength, gait, sit-to-stand, dexterity, balance.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Perfusion state, BP, function, fatigue and workload; atenolol limits HR interpretation.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ILMB intervention</b><p>Task-specific rehab only where measurable reserve/deficit exists.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat identical functional tests after a defined rehab block.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Equality test</b><p>Functional output maintained/improved without new neurologic events; antiplatelet equivalence remains unproven.</p></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>05</b><strong>Nutrient requirement</strong><span>Same biochemical need, exact chemical amount</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Baseline</b><p>Repeat 25-OH-D; TSH + free T4; need-specific nutrient markers.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Input map</b><p>Verify cod-liver-oil and Neurobion formulations + current food intake.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>ILMB intervention</b><p>Calculate only the missing chemical amount after total intake and safety context are known.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Re-measure</b><p>Repeat the relevant biomarker.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Equality test</b><p>Deficiency/requirement corrected without excess.</p></div></div></details>
</div><div class="call"><b>The rule for Nilesh:</b> if the pharmacy endpoint is measurable, ILMB must be judged against that same endpoint. If the endpoint cannot yet be shown equivalent—especially antiplatelet recurrence protection—the dashboard must say so instead of pretending equality has been established.</div></div></section>
<section id="reports" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">MY REPORTS</div><h2>What happened and what is known now</h2><div class="timeline"><div class="event"><div><b>23 Aug 2024</b><p>MRI brain</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Multiple fresh non-haemorrhagic right fronto-parieto-temporal infarcts.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Several right-brain regions were injured because blood supply failed.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>23 Aug 2024</b><p>MRA</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>High-grade right MCA occlusion from origin; severe distal paucity.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Main arterial route to a large right-brain territory was severely compromised.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>21 Jul 2025</b><p>MRI/MRA</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Right MCA M1 no flow; faint M2 enhancement possibly collateral.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Vessel abnormality persisted; collateral supply may exist but was not quantified.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>26 Jul 2025</b><p>Clinical follow-up</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Normal speech; no recorded deficit.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Function recovered more than vessel imaging alone suggests.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>31 Jul 2026</b><p>Plain CT</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Old right-sided infarcts; no acute infarct, haemorrhage or mass.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>No new acute lesion; current MCA lumen/collateral reserve/perfusion still unresolved.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="numbers" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">MEASUREMENTS</div><h2>Numbers that drive the Pharmacy = ILMB comparison</h2><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><small>Triglycerides</small><strong>301 mg/dL</strong><small>LOINC 2571-8</small></div><div class="metric"><small>ALT</small><strong>81 U/L</strong><small>LOINC 1742-6</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Creatinine</small><strong>1.27 mg/dL</strong><small>LOINC 2160-0</small></div><div class="metric"><small>eGFR</small><strong>72</strong><small>Kidney context</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Potassium</small><strong>5.3 mmol/L</strong><small>LOINC 2823-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Platelets</small><strong>133 ×10³/µL</strong><small>LOINC 777-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>25-OH Vitamin D</small><strong>13.9 ng/mL</strong><small>LOINC 62292-8</small></div><div class="metric"><small>TSH</small><strong>5.386</strong><small>LOINC 3016-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>HbA1c</small><strong>5.8%</strong><small>LOINC 4548-4</small></div></div><div class="call"><b>Still unresolved:</b> current right-MCA flow/perfusion/collaterals, repeat fasting labs, quantitative motor baseline, and exact cod-liver-oil/Neurobion chemistry.</div></div></section>
<section id="science" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">BACKGROUND</div><h2>The database stays behind the patient story</h2><div class="flow"><span class="node">Pharmacy endpoint</span><span class="arr">=</span><span class="node">Required physiological output</span><span class="arr">=</span><span class="node">ILMB endpoint</span></div><div class="flow" style="margin-top:10px"><span class="node">Patient result</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">LOINC</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Body state</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">ChEBI</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Reactome</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">ILMB input</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Re-measure same endpoint</span></div><div class="call"><b>Governance:</b> no same-endpoint measurement = no equality claim. Unknown is never converted to zero. Different mechanism is acceptable; invented equivalence is not.</div></div></section>
</div></main><script>const bs=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-panel]')],ps=[...document.querySelectorAll('.panel')];function show(id){bs.forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.panel===id));ps.forEach(p=>p.classList.toggle('active',p.id===id));history.replaceState(null,'','#'+id)}bs.forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>show(b.dataset.panel));const h=location.hash.slice(1);if(document.getElementById(h))show(h);</script></body></html>